==============================================================================
 [2] SIGPIPE: set_signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN) + EPIPE/ECONNRESET in write_n
==============================================================================
Scenario: 3 clients subscribe (push every 200 ms) and disconnect after 1 push.

--- WITHOUT ---
$ ./server -p 9090 --no-sigpipe
$ ./client --mode abort --abort-after 1   x 3 (subscribe, then disconnect)
server log, child exits:
  23:34:56.045 [server:26145] WARN  reaped child 26155: killed by signal 13 (Broken pipe) | active=2
  23:34:56.047 [server:26145] WARN  reaped child 26156: killed by signal 13 (Broken pipe) | active=1
  23:34:56.048 [server:26145] WARN  reaped child 26157: killed by signal 13 (Broken pipe) | active=0
children killed by SIGPIPE: 3 | children that handled EPIPE (exit 4): 0
server parent alive: yes | next normal client exit status: 0

--- WITH ---
$ ./server -p 9090 
$ ./client --mode abort --abort-after 1   x 3 (subscribe, then disconnect)
server log, child exits:
  23:34:57.703 [server:26175] WARN  127.0.0.1:45450: push #3 failed: Broken pipe -> client gone, exiting cleanly
  23:34:57.704 [server:26176] WARN  127.0.0.1:45458: push #3 failed: Broken pipe -> client gone, exiting cleanly
  23:34:57.705 [server:26165] INFO  reaped child 26175: exit 4 (client gone, EPIPE/ECONNRESET handled) | active=2
  23:34:57.706 [server:26165] INFO  reaped child 26176: exit 4 (client gone, EPIPE/ECONNRESET handled) | active=1
  23:34:57.706 [server:26177] WARN  127.0.0.1:45462: push #3 failed: Broken pipe -> client gone, exiting cleanly
  23:34:57.708 [server:26165] INFO  reaped child 26177: exit 4 (client gone, EPIPE/ECONNRESET handled) | active=0
children killed by SIGPIPE: 0 | children that handled EPIPE (exit 4): 3
server parent alive: yes | next normal client exit status: 0

--- Checks [2] ---
  [PASS] without: 3 children killed by signal 13 (SIGPIPE)
  [PASS] with: 0 children killed by SIGPIPE
  [PASS] with: 3 children saw EPIPE and exited cleanly (exit 4)
  [PASS] with: the server keeps serving new clients

